"""PyInstaller freeze spec for VYUK — Wave 10 (v5.65) Leaf 1.

Build (on Windows only; see WINDOWS_BUILD_CHECKLIST.md):
    cd <build-dir>\\voice_assistant
    pyinstaller --noconfirm --clean installer\\vyuk.spec
Output: dist\\vyuk\\vyuk.exe (onedir) + dist\\vyuk\\_internal\\...

Build-box layout, and why it matters: main.py imports
``voice_assistant.core`` / ``voice_assistant.gui``. In the source
tree the package IS the tree root (exposed under the name
``voice_assistant``), so for PyInstaller's analysis to resolve those
imports, the tree folder itself must be named ``voice_assistant``
inside the build dir, and pathex must be that build dir. The spec
derives both from its own location, so it works from any cwd as
long as the folder name is right; the checklist stages it so.

Datas — placed where the FROZEN code actually looks, not where the
source tree keeps them (verified against the source, 2026-10-25):

* assets/ -> 'assets' (dist root): core/voice/local_assets.py's frozen
  branch resolves bundled assets as <exe_dir>/assets, and the OCR
  tessdata lives under assets/ocr/.
* gui/assets/ -> '_internal/gui/assets': gui/style.py and
  gui/sounds.py resolve gui assets from Path(__file__).parent /
  'assets', and under a frozen onedir build gui modules live in
  _internal/gui/. (If a future PyInstaller changes the frozen
  module layout, the Windows smoke check — fonts actually load —
  catches it; see the checklist.)
* plugins/ -> '_internal/plugins': core/plugin_loader.py resolves
  PLUGINS_DIR from its own file's parent's parent, i.e. _internal
  when frozen. Shipping the whole directory carries the two plugin
  .py files AND plugins_hashes.json + .sig beside them, which the
  loader's hash verification requires.

Deliberately NOT bundled:

* data/ — user data (assistant.db, logs, voices, milestones) is
  created by the app at first run (core/config.py mkdirs DATA_DIR).
  Shipping a data/ snapshot would bake one machine's history into
  every install. The installer never ships it; the uninstaller
  only deletes it on the user's explicit delete-my-data choice
  (PF-24, see vyuk.iss [Code]).
* icon — Phase G (Command Deck, D7): the S1 mark ships as
  gui/assets/vyuk_icon.png (512 master, diamond frame + core +
  single ring, generated by installer/make_vyuk_icon.py) and as
  the multi-size gui/assets/vyuk.ico (16/20/24/32/40/48/64/128/
  256). icon= below points at the .ico, and vyuk.iss sets
  SetupIconFile to the same file.

console=False: this is the GUI build — no console window behind
the app. upx=False: UPX is not a guaranteed build-box tool, and a
missing UPX must not fail the freeze.
"""

